  "reason": "The source assertion defines the relationship as 'receive incoming signals at', where dendrites acquire signals from synapses. The proposed assertion defines the relationship as 'uses_to_transmit_signals_to', implying dendrites employ synapses as a mechanism to reach target cells. This reverses the semantic direction: in the source, synapses are the location/source of reception; in the proposal, synapses are treated as the tool/mechanism used by dendrites to transmit outward. The proposed definition incorrectly attributes the transmission action to the dendrite using the synapse, whereas the biological fact (and source text) is that dendrites receive signals *at* synapses, not that they use synapses to transmit signals elsewhere."
